{
  "format": "lumeri.interface/v1",
  "id": "iface:storyboard.edit/v1",
  "version": "1.1.0",
  "area": "tools",
  "title": "Write and assemble the storyboard",
  "summary": "Replace a storyboard, update a shot, assemble filled shots onto a track, or refine a placed shot and its clip together. The package owns shotlist.json and delegates timeline validation to the Runtime.",
  "carrier": {
    "kind": "luc-protocol",
    "protocol": "lumeri.tool/v2",
    "surface": "packaged-agent-tool",
    "notes": "Operations describe the capability result before the luc_invoke identity wrapper and model-result clipping."
  },
  "replaceability": {
    "class": "sandboxed",
    "why": "The package carries Python code the Runtime runs, so its own files stay as they shipped. A creator's layer may add a program that answers for a capability instead: it runs only in the code sandbox, reaches the Project only through ToolHost's calls over its pipe, and is held to this contract (docs/luc/tool-programs.md).",
    "decided": "self-Luc spec v0.3 (2026-10-18); today's code: lumeri_runtime/luc_packaged_tools.py:545-561; Acrab 2026-10-26: replaced by programs in the code sandbox"
  },
  "reach": {
    "permissions": [
      "project.read",
      "project.write"
    ],
    "host_apis": [
      "project.read",
      "document.edit"
    ],
    "editable": {
      "target_types": [
        "project_document"
      ],
      "properties": [
        "document.content"
      ],
      "areas": [
        "project"
      ]
    }
  },
  "operations": [
    {
      "name": "edit_storyboard",
      "capability": "storyboard.edit",
      "effect": "write",
      "input": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "op": {
            "enum": [
              "set_shotlist",
              "update_shot",
              "assemble_shotlist",
              "refine_shot"
            ],
            "description": "set_shotlist replaces the storyboard; update_shot rewrites one shot; assemble_shotlist lays every shot that has footage down as clips; refine_shot retimes, refills or removes one shot that is already laid down."
          },
          "data": {
            "type": "object",
            "description": "set_shotlist: {shotlist: {logline, style, target_duration_sec, scenes: [{id, title, shots}]}}. update_shot: {shot}.",
            "properties": {
              "shot": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                  "id": {
                    "type": "string"
                  },
                  "clip_id": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  },
                  "description": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "What this beat shows."
                  },
                  "duration_sec": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "exclusiveMinimum": 0
                  },
                  "on_screen_text": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  },
                  "narration": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  },
                  "mood": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  },
                  "source": {
                    "enum": [
                      "generate",
                      "search",
                      "unset"
                    ]
                  },
                  "search_query": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  },
                  "asset_id": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ],
                    "description": "The footage that fills the shot, once chosen."
                  },
                  "transition_after": {
                    "type": [
                      "object",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  },
                  "status": {
                    "enum": [
                      "draft",
                      "filled",
                      "placed"
                    ]
                  },
                  "notes": {
                    "type": [
                      "string",
                      "null"
                    ]
                  }
                },
                "required": [
                  "id"
                ]
              },
              "shotlist": {
                "type": "object"
              }
            }
          },
          "shot_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "update_shot and refine_shot: the shot."
          },
          "track_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "assemble_shotlist: the track to lay onto (V1)."
          },
          "start_at": {
            "type": "number",
            "minimum": 0,
            "description": "assemble_shotlist: where to begin."
          },
          "duration_sec": {
            "type": "number",
            "exclusiveMinimum": 0,
            "description": "refine_shot: a new length."
          },
          "asset_id": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "refine_shot: other footage, same place."
          },
          "remove": {
            "const": true,
            "description": "refine_shot: take the shot back off."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "op"
        ]
      },
      "output": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "shotlist": {
            "$contract": "contracts/interfaces/tools/storyboard.edit.v1.json#/definitions/shotlist"
          },
          "project_revision": {
            "type": "integer"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "shotlist",
          "project_revision"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "errors": [
        "arguments_invalid",
        "shotlist_patch_refused",
        "approval_required",
        "document_edit_failed",
        "E_LUC_EDIT_SCOPE",
        "E_LUC_API_UNDECLARED",
        "E_LUC_API_PERMISSION",
        "E_LUC_API_UNAVAILABLE",
        "E_LUC_PROGRAM_BROKE"
      ],
      "deadline_ms": null,
      "idempotency": "idempotency_key",
      "status": "defined",
      "evidence": [
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:143-194",
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:351-429",
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:535-578",
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_packaged_tools.py:405-452",
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_host_api.py:590-602"
      ],
      "notes": "No end-to-end call deadline is enforced. Retrying with the Runtime-derived key reuses the same write. A fresh assemble call refuses clip ids already placed; refining duration reflows later clips, replacing an asset preserves position, and remove returns the shot to intent. The result returns the storyboard, not the timeline changed alongside it."
    }
  ],
  "events": [
    {
      "name": "luc.module_fell_back",
      "payload": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "module": {
            "const": "lumeri.shotlist"
          },
          "layer": {
            "type": "object",
            "properties": {
              "id": {
                "type": "string"
              },
              "version": {
                "type": "string"
              }
            },
            "required": [
              "id",
              "version"
            ],
            "additionalProperties": false
          },
          "gate": {
            "const": "run"
          },
          "code": {
            "type": "string"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "module",
          "layer",
          "gate",
          "code"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_tool_program.py:267-303"
      ],
      "notes": "Once per Session in a start, when a layer's program broke and the Official code answers instead."
    }
  ],
  "bounds": [
    {
      "name": "agent_result_chars",
      "value": 6000,
      "unit": "characters before the model result is clipped; the cut notice is appended",
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/agent_turn.py:38-42",
        "lumeri_runtime/agent_turn.py:423-430"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "scenes",
      "value": 512,
      "unit": "scenes per storyboard",
      "evidence": [
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:36-39"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "shots_per_scene",
      "value": 512,
      "unit": "shots",
      "evidence": [
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:36-39"
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "shot_seconds",
      "value": 3600,
      "unit": "seconds",
      "evidence": [
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:36-39"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "invariants": [
    {
      "id": "host-keeps-authority",
      "text": "The Runtime authorizes declared Host APIs and checks the tool edit scope before a Project mutation; the package cannot expand its effective editable boundary.",
      "test": null
    },
    {
      "id": "placed-shot-has-clip",
      "text": "An assembled shot is marked placed with the id of the clip created for it.",
      "test": "tests/test_runtime_shotlist.py::test_both_documents_move_together"
    }
  ],
  "failure": {
    "break": [
      "A layer's program does not start, answers late, too large or out of shape, or ends.",
      "It asks for a host call that does not exist, with other arguments, or more than 256 of them.",
      "Its result does not keep the output schema, or its refusal names an error code not listed here."
    ],
    "fallback": "original",
    "evidence": [
      "lumeri_runtime/luc_tool_program.py:169-223",
      "lumeri_runtime/luc_tool_program.py:234-265",
      "lumeri_runtime/luc_packaged_tools.py:610-622"
    ],
    "notes": "The Official code answers the same call, and every call of this Luc for the rest of the start; the Session hears luc.module_fell_back once and luc_breaker counts one break. A call whose program had already changed something is refused with E_LUC_PROGRAM_BROKE instead, and what changed stands. Without a program, a call that raises or refuses reaches the agent as a refusal."
  },
  "conformance": {
    "status": "partial",
    "tests": [
      "tests/test_runtime_shotlist.py",
      "tests/test_luc_tool_program.py"
    ],
    "notes": "Existing behavior tests cover parts of this interface. They were inspected, not run in this documentation task; no replacement conformance runner exists yet. tests/test_luc_tool_program.py holds a replacement to this interface: the load gate, the answers the Runtime accepts, and the fallback to the Official code."
  },
  "known_deviations": [
    {
      "text": "The loaded capability advertises only an object output schema. Its actual structured result below is not enforced by the current adapter.",
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_packaged_tools.py:565-566",
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_packaged_tools.py:624-627"
      ],
      "test": null
    },
    {
      "text": "draft_shotlist, legacy source-range/evidence fields and recaptioning are not ported. Assembly refuses a requested transition rather than dropping it.",
      "evidence": [
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:41-66",
        "official_luc/shotlist/tools.py:378-385"
      ],
      "test": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Only the agent's call goes to a layer's program. Where the editor asks a packaged tool directly through the Worker's own routes, the Official code answers.",
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/worker.py:3129-3132",
        "lumeri_runtime/worker.py:3913-3927"
      ],
      "test": null
    },
    {
      "text": "Stopping the turn does not stop a program mid-call; the 10 s deadline per answer and the bound of 256 host calls end it.",
      "evidence": [
        "lumeri_runtime/luc_tool_program.py:169-223"
      ],
      "test": null
    }
  ],
